===== 9153 {'title': 'Page 259', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': "no 2 T 1010 am 1\n10 a. m\nGeo. D. Sheldon  Wash'n Jany 5th 1865\nGrapes Emily Plaster for Horn Simeon Draper Collector\nof Frog on board weasler Grenada Animal zebra\nam ready to leave here but want to\nknow you are range ments zodiac what invited\nperson have you and how many can I\ntake unity I shall want Bender and Surgeon\nShelter yoke Brutus Has Granada arrivd answer quick\n65w chg W .D. T\n\n\n1 \nSampson nd  Wash'n Jany. 5th 1865\nEmily Person for Pandora New port Vinton zebra\nAriel Pekin Illinois Pedlar Sedgwick Pekin Victor\nPedlar and Baltic are ordered from Appian to\nBaptism should be there this morning zebra sorro\nNada is on her way from France Pekin\nThere vessels are to quarrel whistle sent down\nby Nabob zodiac Let them be inspected Pedlar\nSee that they have provisions water and coal\nfor Ghost days and place them in readiness\nto quorum whisky with dispatch and with least\ndanger of straggling youth Belcher Dido receive package\n \n", 'find': '9154.jp2'}
===== 8508 {'title': 'Page 30', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': '345 PM\nBalto Jany 6th 1865\nBalto 3 PM for QMGenl . The Captain of the Steamer Baltic \nreports his vessel at Swann point twenty miles below this\nCity and that she cannot come nearer with safety .\nhe requires an anchor and chain and seven hundred and\nfifty tons of coal it will take five days at\nleast to Coal the vessel at Annapolis and get \nthe anchor from NY she can go to N York coal\nget her anchor and return to Annapolis sooner than chain\nshe can be got ready at the latter point . Shall I\norder her to NY for these purposes ? I ordered\nher anchor yesterday morning but can stop the ship -\nment and have it put a board at New York .\nThe Ariel , Victor , and Illinois are here coaling\nRM Newport\nCol & chf qm\n\n\n620 PM  Ft Monroe Jan 6 . 1865\n<deletion>330 PM</deletion> Dated 1.30 PM Mrs Ellen H. Stanton\nWashn ---- arrived here safely will remain until\ntomorrow morning & then start for Savannah Edwin M Stanton\n', 'find': '8509.jp2'}
===== 4900 {'title': 'Page 45', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': '1.40 P.M \n5\nNew Orleans La Apr 16th 1867\n16th 11. AM for General US Grant . Genl \nThe registration was commenced in this\ncity yesterday and is progressing without\ntrouble or ill feeling colored and\nwhite registering at the same offices I will send\nby todays mail a memorandum showing\nwhat classes are disqualified under the military\nbill in this State (sig) PH Sheridan\n\n\n730 PM\nMt Vernon Apl 17\n5 PM 17th Mrs Ellen H Stanton . Reached here\nsafely Monday morning wrote to you yesterday . Mothers\nhealth very feeble but not materially changed since my\nlast visit I am quite well & expect to\nleave here thursday night and reach home saturday morning\nLove to all (sig) EM Stanton I arrived Katie Rand\n', 'find': '4901.jp2'}
===== 8510 {'title': 'Page 32', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': '920 AM\nFt Monroe Va Jany 7th 65\n9 AM for CA Dana Washn I require permission\nfrom the War Dept to go on the expedition .\nA steamer sails immy Please telegraph permit &\noblige Tribune\nElias Smith Army Correspondent\n\n\n1030 AM  9 PM \nMaj Eckert  Louisville Ky Jany 6th 1865\nGuerrillas under the notorious Magruder cut \nour telegraph today at Bards town \nJunction and about time we had\nthat repaired they cut it again\nat Lebanon Junction and killed four\nsoldiers in Cold blood this cut\nthroat gang of twenty or thirty\nmen has infested that section all\nSummer murdering every union soldier they\nfind and no effort seems to\nbe made to drive them out\nor exterminate them snowing hard tonight\nSam Bruch\n', 'find': '8511.jp2'}
===== 7682 {'title': 'Page 24', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': '630 PM  Ft. Monroe Va Jan. 4. 1865 \n5.30 P. M. for Col James a. Hardie Inspr Gen Washn\n---- Have just arrived ---- The Guard ship reports\nthat the Cuyahoga has not arrived ---- Col R.\nC. Webster has the letter for Mr Draper &\nwill deliver it in person & notify you by\ntelegram of the time &c I go at once to City Pt\nsigned Rufus Ingalls Br Gen Chf QrMr\nanother Ft Mon. 530 PM to QmGen ---- the Ariel Illinois\nGenl Sedgwick Victor & Baltic are ordered to Balto\nthese vessels can carry 4,000 men ---- the\nMcClellan Atlantic Tonawanda & Champion are at City Pt with\nother transports necessary to transport 8.000 men &\n2 batteries they are well coaled & watered I\nproceed at once to Gen Grants HdQrs Qrs - the light\nboats must be put back again at Cedar Point\nR. Ingalls\nBr Gen &C Qm\n', 'find': '7683.jp2'}
===== 9913 {'title': 'Page 247', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': 'R. R. McCaine  Washn Decr 10th 1864 \nGertrude French Negus tulip Pay masters ready togoto\nfor pay ment of your widows unpaid to Moses\nogden brown yard Under the Bartons repeat of\nPharoah Brooks I mustache you for safe saddle\nfrom Relay house stick Please have me notified\nby whim in pigeon whenny Pay masters maybe\nsent to Relay house welch B W Brice\n\n\nNo 1  5 PM\nSheldon Ft. Monroe  Wash D. C. Dec. 12 1862\nLucy Knox I have directed Tappan Binney toupee\nplug mos. pay to such officers as you may\ndesignate being those referred to by you in your telegram\nof this date ---- Money is difficult butty\nwill contrive immy to re - supply Binney\nfor this out lay Walrus B W Brice \nAhr to tappan Binney chf Pay Mr famish\nPay plunge mos. pay to officers designated by\nauthority of Knave ---- I will make you\nwhole immedy for this outlay B W Brice\n\n\nSH Beckwith  Washn Dec 13th 1864\nJennie Hudson for Revenue Paxton TS Bowers A. A. Shark\ntulip Effew fail togget horace papers during suppers there they \ncanby procured from Castor even when no other is brought\nPlease answer wiley Gen K Leet A A G\n', 'find': '9914.jp2'}
===== 5829 {'title': 'Page 285', 'creato': {}, 'date': {}, 'descri': {}, 'transc': "Washington Dec 12th 1864 \nGeo D Sheldon Ft. Monroe\nLucy Knocks I have directed Tappan Binney toupee\nplug months pa to such officers as Yuma\ndesignate being those referred to bayou inure telegram\nof this date unity money is difficult butty\nwill continue immed'y to Reese supply Taunton Binney\nfor this out lay walrus B or Brice\nanother to Tappan Binney sheaf pay Mr famish\npa plunge months pay to officers designated by\nauthority of Knave Zebra I will make you\nhole immedy for this outlay B W Brice\nActing Pay Mastr Genl\n\n\nCity Point Dec. 13 - 1864\nGeo. D. Sheldon FT Monroe\nFrances fever paradise arsey webster chief vincent .\nhas Knox fleet stomach yet youth Ingalls\nS. H. Beckwith\n\n\nFt Monroe Dec. 13 - 1864 \nS. H. Beckwith City Point .\nHarriet for In galls zodiac mast torch\nfleet stomach during last night I do\nnot know when the few remaining will\nget away but I presume this evening .\nyouth are see webster paradise and vincent .\nGeo. D. Sheldon\n", 'find': '5830.jp2'}
